aleontological, and geological collections. Students gain insight into the nature and importance of collections and explore the profession within the modern collections landscape. Focus placed on comparison of collections, with practical hands-on experience in the University of Illinois’s scientific surveys (ISAS, INHS, and ISGS). Topics covered include physical curation and conservation of collections objects (specimens and artifacts), digital imaging and databasing, and data management.","title":"Scientific Collections"},{"crn":"44851","code":"PAN","type":"Online","partOfTerm":"B","meetings":[{"type":"Online","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"","instructors":["Allan, B"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Pandemics (global outbreaks of infectious disease) are among the most impactful events in human history. Through this course, we will study the major historical and modern pandemics from an advanced biological as well as social and political perspectives. We will compare past pandemics to the public health crisis caused by COVID-19, and we will apply this knowledge to interpret scientific discoveries related to future pandemics and their prevention.","title":"Pandemics"},{"crn":"78948","code":"PD1","type":"Online Discussion","partOfTerm":"B","meetings":[{"type":"Online Discussion","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"","instructors":["Allan, B"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"","title":"Pandemics"},{"crn":"78947","code":"PD2","type":"Online Discussion","partOfTerm":"B","meetings":[{"type":"Online Discussion","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"","instructors":["Allan, B"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"","title":"Pandemics"},{"crn":"78946","code":"PD3","type":"Online Discussion","partOfTerm":"B","meetings":[{"type":"Online Discussion","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"","instructors":["Allan, B"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"","title":"Pandemics"}]},{"id":"IB 497","title":"Science Communication","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours.","sections